NOTE: httpx / PyJWT / cryptography are used by the M365 (ne/connect/m365), Slack
(ne/connect/slack) and Salesforce (ne/connect/salesforce) thin HTTP clients —
app-only/connected-app OAuth token flows (cert-signed or JWT-bearer assertions,
client-credentials) over a small, SSRF-guarded httpx surface. They are already
pinned+hash-verified in the workspace uv.lock via sibling packages (ne-identity /
ne-permissions), so none of NE-044/045/047 add a new lock entry. The Entra/
Salesforce client-credential + assertion-signing patterns follow the in-repo
ne-permissions entra.py precedent — no external code was lifted.

