NOTE (NE-047 Salesforce connector, ne/connect/salesforce): adds ZERO new
third-party components — no new lock entry, no new line above. It reuses the
existing httpx/PyJWT/cryptography pins for its thin REST/Bulk API 2.0 client
and connected-app OAuth (JWT-bearer/client-credentials) flows. simple-salesforce
(1.12.9, Apache-2.0 — corrected from the orchestrator brief's "MIT"; verified
2026-07-06) was evaluated during planning and NOT adopted: it is a synchronous,
requests-based transport, which would bypass the C2 egress guardian's import
allowlist (`requests` is a forbidden top-level import under ne/connect), the
per-request SSRF/instance-pinning re-validation, the AIR_GAP construction
guard, and the mandated httpx.MockTransport fixture-first CI (NE-000) — the
same build-vs-adopt call NE-045 made for `slack_sdk` (see that unit's commit
message). No dlt Salesforce source is used either: dlt has no importable
in-package Salesforce source (only a vendored `dlt init` scaffold built on
simple-salesforce), so it inherits the same disqualifying issues; the
connector plugs into the dlt-based NE-040 framework (bridge/state/contracts)
without adding a fourth dlt import site.

NOTE (NE-093 Jira + Zendesk connectors, ne/connect/jira + ne/connect/zendesk):
add ZERO new third-party components — no new lock entry, no new line above. Both
reuse the already-recorded httpx surface for their thin Basic-auth REST clients
(no atlassian/zendesk SDKs, no dlt import). atlassian-python-api and zenpy were
evaluated during planning and NOT adopted: both are synchronous, requests-based
transports (and zenpy is GPL-family, which would additionally require
out-of-process isolation under C4) that would bypass the C2 egress guardian's
import allowlist (`requests` is a forbidden top-level import under ne/connect),
the per-request SSRF/path-guard re-validation, the AIR_GAP construction guard,
and the mandated httpx.MockTransport fixture-first CI (NE-000) — the same
build-vs-adopt call NE-045 made for slack_sdk and NE-047 for simple-salesforce.
The dlt-hub verified-sources jira/zendesk templates (Apache-2.0) are consulted
as endpoint/resource-semantics REFERENCE ONLY (they are requests-based +
dlt-pipeline-coupled), never vendored, so this unit adds no fourth dlt import
site either.

NOTE (NE-080 Microsoft Teams connector, ne/connect/teams): adds ZERO new
third-party components — no new lock entry, no new line above. It reuses the
